<title>FRANCE: French communists seek Thomson sale probe.</title>
<headline>French communists seek Thomson sale probe.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French communist group in the lower house National Assembly called on Thursday for a committee of inquiry to be set up to look into the privatisation of electronics firm Thomson SA.</p>
<p>The communist Assembly members, led by Alain Bocquet, formally asked for the inquiry &quot;into the situation of the Thomson group and the conditions of its privatisation,&quot; a statement fron the communist group said.</p>
<p>The communist move follows a similar call by the leader of the socialist group, Laurent Fabius, on Wednesday. Both groups oppose the privatisation and the sale of the Thomson-CSF unit.</p>
</text>
